   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize Patrick Cechnicki to take the competitive civil service examination and be placed on the eligible list for appointment as a full-time police officer for the village of Fort Plain, county of Montgomery",
    "basePrintNo": "S6332",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6332-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6332\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to authorize Patrick Cechnicki to take the\ncompetitive civil service examination and be placed on the eligible\nlist for appointment as a full-time police officer for the village of\nFort Plain, county of Montgomery\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nAuthorizes Patrick Cechnicki to take the competitive exam for police\nofficer and be placed on the eligible list for such position in the\nvillage of Fort Plain.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Authorizes Patrick Cechnicki to sit for the civil service\nexam and be placed on the eligibility list for full time police\nofficer for the village of Fort Plain.\n\nSection 2: Patrick Cechnick is subject to the merit and fitness\nprovisions of the civil service law applicable to full-time officers.\n\nSection 3: Establishes the effective date as immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nUnder the Civil Service Law, as proscribed under Section 58, no\nindividual may take the civil service examination, nor be eligible for\na civil service appointment as a police officer, at the age of 35 or\nolder. Due to this limitation, the village of Fort Plain Police\nDepartment has requested legislation to permit one of their part-time\nofficers, Patrick Cechnicki, to be eligible to take the civil service\nexamination since he is currently older than 35 years old.\n\nIn small rural areas, it is difficult to attract or maintain qualified\napplicants to fill such positions. Upon Patrick Cechnicki passing the\nexamination, this would qualify him to fill the vacant full-time\nposition within the village of Fort Plain Police Department.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nTo be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
